From: baseband lane
Subject: 0505 pandora_mpss: the AOP mailbox's box is 8-byte aligned, not 16 -- zero it byte-wise

Step 3 of the modem bring-up died with "Unaligned kernel data abort" (esr 0x96000061,
far = mp_qmp + 0x38, pc = _step_mailbox + 0x18c) on the first hardware run, 2026-11-21.

QMP_OUR_BOX is offset 0x38 of the mailbox mapping, so the box is 8-byte aligned but not 16.
`memset(box, 0, QMP_MESSAGE)` is a 64-byte zeroing that clang vectorises into 16-byte NEON
stores; this kernel runs with strict alignment, so the first `stp q` faults.  Replaced with a
byte loop through a volatile pointer, which cannot be misaligned whatever the compiler does.

Evidence: the fault dump in device/private/logs/1795238956 (step 4 run) - steps 1 and 2 had
already passed on hardware ("the firmware is whole: ... ends 0x98200000 with 0x900000 to spare"),
and PANDORA PAS never printed, which localises the fault to step 3.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index e8f25f8..b937dc6 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -718,9 +718,25 @@ mp_mailbox_send(const char *text)
 	if (len >= QMP_MESSAGE) {
 		len = QMP_MESSAGE - 1;
 	}
-	uint8_t *box = (uint8_t *)(mp_qmp + QMP_OUR_BOX);
-	memset(box, 0, QMP_MESSAGE);
-	memcpy(box, text, len);
+	/*
+	 * Byte-wise through a volatile pointer, deliberately.
+	 *
+	 * The mailbox's box is at offset 0x38 of the mapping, so it is 8-byte aligned but NOT
+	 * 16-byte aligned.  `memset(box, 0, 64)` is a 64-byte zeroing that clang vectorises into
+	 * 16-byte NEON stores (`stp q0, q1`), and this kernel runs with strict alignment: the very
+	 * first store faults with "Unaligned kernel data abort", esr 0x96000061, far = box + 0.
+	 * That is exactly what happened on 2026-11-21 at step 3 (pc _step_mailbox + 0x18c), and it
+	 * is why step 4 never reached its TrustZone call.
+	 *
+	 * A byte loop cannot be misaligned whatever the compiler does with it.
+	 */
+	volatile uint8_t *box = (volatile uint8_t *)(mp_qmp + QMP_OUR_BOX);
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < QMP_MESSAGE; i++) {
+		box[i] = 0;
+	}
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < len; i++) {
+		box[i] = (uint8_t)text[i];
+	}
 	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
 	mp_wr(mp_ipcc, IPCC_SEND, 0u << 16 | 0u);       /* IPCC client 0 (the AOP), signal 0 */
 	printf("PANDORA MPSS: told the AOP: %s\n", text);
